  "notes": [
    "The initial editor-popout mock returned an obsolete editor snapshot after save; it now returns the saved note, while the production refresh remains unchanged.",
    "Clippy removed a cloned single-reference slice. Script lint requires explicit globalThis APIs.",
    "Chromium paints textarea glyphs inside its user-agent shadow tree; font audits now inspect those real nodes with frontend CDP node IDs. No computed-family fallback is accepted.",
    "A stale screenshot option label was corrected to the actual accessible name. Visual review caught the shared 200px card width; stickies now use the full inner width and assert it.",
    "Discard decisions trap focus, make other controls inert and hide covered content so default axe can resolve contrast. The explicit failed-close attempt performs one additional snapshot read; the suite checks that exact count.",
    "Earlier and superseded attempts remain archived. Only the delivery screenshot prefix and accepted native/flow reports are authoritative.",
    "Native smoke found that Tao retained caption style bits while extending the client area; it now checks actual client insets and decoration state. The first show also reapplied extended styles and cleared alpha; alpha is now restored after show and relevant native events. A Win32 RECT/POINT probe requires explicit zero fields. Copy packet freezing advances the journal sequence to defeat older pending checkpoints. The bounded recovery journal fits two 3 MB cards plus the frozen copy packet, including future item fields. Reload, discard and copy transitions lock edits and ignore late replies after unmount; undo clears its obsolete journal. The restored HWND can be ready before CDP attaches its target, so the driver waits for that specific owned page before asserting stale-instance rejection. The release candidate began before the final frontend build; the accepted release was rerun after a completed build and its embedded sticky entry is matched to that manifest.",
    "The public bridge log is normalized for trailing whitespace; its exact original bytes remain in the deterministic gzip archive. Windows documentation helpers use explicit UTF-8.",
    "The initial strict scan flagged two random optimistic-edit UUIDs in the authoritative native report. Those unused values are omitted from public evidence; the native verifier now omits them by default. The exact unredacted synthetic report is retained only in ignored local scratch, and the unchanged staged/archive scanner is rerun."
  ],
